1.1.text:
Article 15
(1) In implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women, Regional Governments may conduct cooperation with International Institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
Article 16
The Regent in implementing policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women shall undertake efforts to:
a. coordinate the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women among Regional Apparatus Work Units;
b. cooperate with Regencies/Cities within one Province, and cooperation between Regencies/Cities in other Provinces in the implementation of policies, programs, and activities for the protection of women in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
c. strengthen institutional capacity for gender mainstreaming for the implementation of policies, programs and activities for the protection of women;
d. facilitate protection services for women;
e. provide protection services for women;
f. implement affirmative action for the protection of women; and
g. formulate a data system for the protection of women.

Article 17
(1) The provision of protection services for women as referred to in Article 16 letter e shall be in the form of victim identification, legal assistance, medical rehabilitation, psychosocial rehabilitation, social reintegration, repatriation assistance, or other forms.
(2) The provision of protection services for women referred to in paragraph (1) shall be provided for women who are:
a. victims of violence;
b. victims of human trafficking;
c. in conflict-prone and disaster areas;
d. workers;
e. elderly;
f. persons with disabilities;
g. victims of sexual exploitation;
h. heads of households; and
i. other vulnerable groups.

# REGENT OF TAPIN,

Considering: a. that women as an asset of the nation who play a role in the process of continuation and creation of quality generations need to receive guarantees for the fulfillment of their rights and protection from acts of violence and discrimination;

b. that in addition to protection as referred to in letter a, women need to be empowered so that they can actualize their potential optimally to participate in development;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on the Protection and Empowerment of Women;

In View of: 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 8 of 1965 concerning the Establishment of Level II Region Tanah Laut, Level II Region Tapin and Level II Region Tabalong (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1965 Number 51, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 2756);

